Looking at the problem, I need to find all quadruplets $(p, q, r, n)$ of positive integers with $p, q$ prime, $3 \nmid (p+q)$, and $p+q = r(p-q)^n$.

**Answer leak check:** The problem text contains no leaked solutions. Proceeding.

